With judicious use of Elbereth and hit-and-run, you can always kill
mimics, even at level 1. The safest way, of course, is to let your pet
level up until it's a large dog/cat, when it will handily take out
small and large mimics for you (although you might want to be careful
if there are a lot of mimics in the shop, since your pet may get
overwhelmed).

Another strategy is to find mimics by throwing a gold piece down a row
(don't hit the shopkeeper), lure them out of the shop (they'll follow
you as long as they can see you), and then dispatch them with ranged
attacks or just let them re-hide somewhere where they're out of the
way. They're harmless as long you don't wake them up.

If you want to shop but don't want to deal with the mimics at all,
stand on an empty square next to an item you want, engrave Elbereth a
couple of times, then search 20 times. If you don't find a mimic, you
can safely step onto any of the adjacent squares to buy those items.
If you do find a mimic, wait for it to "turn to flee" and then leave
the shop for a while so it will rehide, then start over; any new items
in the shop, or items in different places than they were before, are
mimics and should be avoided. Repeat until you have bought everything
you want. You may need to leave your pet elsewhere for the duration to
keep it from waking the mimics.


